<Slide style={{ width: '1280px', height: '720px', background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative', fontFamily: 'Source Han Sans, Noto Sans CJK SC, sans-serif' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: '100%', height: 60, background: '#0E3F8C' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', padding: '14px 60px' }}>Why this matters in an NYU Shanghai classroom</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 110, left: 60, width: 320, height: 540, padding: 28, background: '#F0F5FC', borderLeft: '4px solid #1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 16 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>OUR SETTING</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 30, fontWeight: 'bold', fontFamily: 'Source Serif Pro, Georgia, serif', color: '#0E3F8C', lineHeight: 1.2 }}>
      One program, two summers, mixed preparation, one shared bet.
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 40, height: 3, background: '#1E4FA8' }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
      The IMA program draws students from across the liberal-arts curriculum. Game Design is not a vocational track — students enroll to learn how to <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>use a system to express an experience</span>.
    </Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 110, right: 60, width: 780, height: 540, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 18 }}>
    {[
      { tag: 'STUDENTS', t: 'Interdisciplinary cohort, mixed coding background', d: 'Many have never written a line of code. All have something they want to express — a frustration, a memory, a practice. The course exists to give that impulse a system.' },
      { tag: 'COURSE MISSION', t: 'Not "game developer" — "systematic expression of experience"', d: 'We treat the game as a structured translation of lived experience. The evaluation question is not "is it fun?" but "did the translation succeed?"' },
      { tag: 'TWO CONSEQUENCES', t: 'AI is welcome — but only within a boundary', d: 'Because coding is not the learning goal, AI assistance is legitimate. Because intent and emotional structure are the learning goal, those cannot be outsourced. The question becomes how to draw the line.' },
    ].map((b, i) => (
      <Box key={i} style={{ flex: 1, padding: 20, background: '#FFFFFF', border: '1px solid #E5E7EB', borderRadius: 8, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 8 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>{b.tag}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230' }}>{b.t}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>{b.d}</Text>
      </Box>
    ))}
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 680, left: 60, right: 60, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Xingchen Zhang · NYU Shanghai · XJTLU 2026 · Panel 11</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>06 / 16</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
